# Pin the display rotation on every boot.
#
# ro.surface_flinger.primary_display_orientation makes landscape the NATURAL
# orientation, which is the important half. But the framework will still rotate
# away from natural if the device-orientation sensor says so, and this is a
# headset - "which way up is the user" is not a question the accelerometer should
# be answering. So auto-rotate is pinned off and rotation pinned to 0.
#
# These are Settings values, which live in /data. Baking them into the
# image alone is not enough: a factory reset wipes /data and they revert.
# Re-applying on every boot is what makes it durable. The proper
# fix is a frameworks default-settings overlay, which needs a source build.
#
# device_provisioned/user_setup_complete are what a setup wizard writes on its
# last page. This image ships no wizard, so without these the framework treats
# the device as mid-setup forever and Pico's launcher keeps trying to start
# Provision. hide_error_dialogs keeps app crash dialogs off the panel - a mono
# crash dialog lands in both eyes and buries whatever was running.

# seclabel is required, not optional. Without it init refuses to start the
# service at all - "does not have a SELinux domain defined" - because a service
# launched from /system/bin/sh as a non-root user has no domain transition in
# policy. Being globally permissive does not help; init bails before that matters.
# policy_control hides the SystemUI bars: on a headset the physical display is
# owned by the panel shell, and a mono nav/status strip drawn across it lands
# in both eyes. The shell's virtual displays have no decorations anyway, so
# nothing the user interacts with loses them.
service pn2_settings /system/bin/sh -c "settings put system accelerometer_rotation 0; settings put system user_rotation 0; settings put global policy_control immersive.full=*; settings put global device_provisioned 1; settings put secure user_setup_complete 1; settings put global hide_error_dialogs 1"
    user root
    group root
    seclabel u:r:shell:s0
    oneshot
    disabled

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    start pn2_settings
